ee\n31\t  (`rootCmd.Find()`) and refuses any name matching a built-in or alias. At\n32\t  runtime, cobra resolves built-ins first — a later-added built-in silently\n33\t  shadows an installed extension; `gh extension exec` is the only recovery.\n34\t- **Subcommands.** `install`, `create`, `list`, `upgrade`, `remove`, `exec`,\n35\t  `browse`, `search`. Update checks run every 24h (suppressible via env).\n36\t  Discovery is via the `gh-extension` GitHub topic; gh does no signing or\n37\t  verification and explicitly disclaims trust.\n38\t\n39\t## Open decisions (defaults proposed)\n40\t\n41\t1. **Trust model** — match gh's: no signing, no allowlist; install prints\n42\t   repo URL with first-time confirmation; `--yes` skips. Revisit if Entire\n43\t   ever ships an official registry.\n44\t2. **Plugin context** — argv passthrough plus a small set of env vars:\n45\t   `ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT`, `ENTIRE_SESSION_ID` (when active),\n46\t   `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DATA_DIR`. No exposed Go SDK; plugins shell back into\n47\t   `entire` for privileged operations.\n48\t3. **Script plugins on Windows** — match gh: route through `sh.exe` for\n49\t   shebang support. Adds a small Windows-only code path; the alternative\n50\t   (Unix-only scripts) breaks parity.\n51\t\n52\t## Package layout\n53\t\n54\t```\n55\tcmd/entire/cli/plugin/\n56\t  manager.go            // discovery, classification, list, paths\n57\t  manager_test.go\n58\t  install_binary.go     // GitHub release asset → download → manifest\n59\t  install_git.go        // git clone path (script plugins)\n60\t  install_local.go      // symlink for `entire plugin install .`\n61\t  install_test.go\n62\t  upgrade.go            // binary: refetch release; git: pull/reset\n63\t  remove.go\n64\t  dispatch.go           // resolve `entire <unknown>` → exec\n65\t  dispatch_unix.go      // direct exec\n66\t  dispatch_windows.go   // sh.exe routing for script plugins\n67\t  dispatch_test.go\n68\t  manifest.go           // YAML schema (binary plugins only)\n69\t  http.go               // GitHub release fetching\n70\t  pin.go                // .pin-<sha> markers\n71\t  create/\n72\t    create.go           // scaffold subcommand\n73\t    templates/\n74\t      go/               // binary plugin scaffold + GH Actions release workflow\n75\t      bash/             // script plugin scaffold\n76\t  testutil/             // fake release server, fake git repo, fake plugin binaries\n77\tcmd/entire/cli/plugin_group.go   // cobra wiring: `entire plugin {…}`\n78\tcmd/entire/cli/plugin_exec.go    // `entire plugin exec <name>`\n79\t```\n80\t\n81\tNaming follows the existing `<noun>_group.go` / `<noun>_<verb>.go`\n82\tconvention from CLAUDE.md.\n83\t\n84\t## CLI surface\n85\t\n86\t```\n87\tentire plugin install <repo>     # owner/name, full URL, or \".\" for local\n88\t                                 # auto-detects: release assets → binary; else git clone\n89\tentire plugin install --pin <ver> <repo>\n90\tentire plugin list               # name, version, kind (binary|script|local), pinned?\n91\tentire plugin upgrade [<name>]   # all if omitted; --force overrides pin\n92\tentire plugin remove <name>\n93\tentire plugin exec <name> [...]  # bypass cobra (escape hatch for collisions)\n94\tentire plugin search <query>     # GitHub topic search: \"entire-plugin\"\n95\tentire plugin browse <name>      # open repo in browser\n96\tentire plugin pin <name> <ver>\n97\tentire plugin create <name> [--precompiled=go|other]\n98\t                                 # default: bash script template\n99\t                                 # --precompiled=go: Go binary + release workflow\n100\t                                 # --precompiled=other: language-agnostic binary scaffold\n101\t```\n102\t\n103\t## Dispatcher wiring\n104\t\n105\tHook in `main.go`'s existing unknown-command branch (`main.go:42-47`).\n106\tReplace the `showSuggestion` call site with: try\n107\t`plugin.Dispatch(rootCmd, os.Args[1:])` first; on miss, fall through to\n108\t`showSuggestion`. Cobra resolves built-ins first → plugins can never shadow\n109\tbuilt-ins. Conflict check at install time uses `rootCmd.Find()` and rejects\n110\tcollisions with built-ins or aliases.\n111\t\n112\t`Dispatch` returns `(handled bool, err error)`; `handled=false` falls through\n113\tto the suggestion path. Keeps the diff in `main.go` minimal and the contract\n114\texplicit.\n115\t\n116\tPer-kind exec:\n117\t\n118\t- **Binary / local** — direct `exec.Command` on Unix and Windows.\n119\t- **Script (git-cloned)** — direct exec on Unix (shebang honored). On\n120\t  Windows, route through `sh.exe` (gh's approach); document the dependency.\n121\t\n122\t## Storage layout\n123\t\n124\t```\n125\t$XDG_DATA_HOME/entire/plugins/        # ~/.local/share/entire/plugins; ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DIR override\n126\t  entire-foo/                         # binary plugin\n127\t    manifest.yml                      # owner, name, host, tag, isPinned, path\n128\t    entire-foo\n129\t    .pin-<sha>                        # optional\n130\t  entire-bar/                         # script plugin (git-cloned)\n131\t    .git/\n132\t    entire-bar                        # executable matching dir name\n133\t    README.md ...                     # repo contents\n134\t  entire-baz                          # local plugin (symlink → /path/to/dev/dir)\n135\t```\n136\t\n137\tClassification on scan: symlink → local; has `manifest.yml` → binary;\n138\totherwise → script.\n139\t\n140\t## Manifest (binary plugins only)\n141\t\n142\t```yaml\n143\towner: octocat\n144\tname: foo\n145\thost: github.com\n146\ttag: v1.2.3\n147\tisPinned: false\n148\tpath: /home/u/.local/share/entire/plugins/entire-foo/entire-foo\n149\t```\n150\t\n151\tField-for-field parity with gh's `binManifest` so intuition transfers.\n152\t\n153\t## Install resolution\n154\t\n155\t`entire plugin install <repo>`:\n156\t\n157\t1. If arg is `.` → local symlink path.\n158\t2. Resolve `<repo>` to GitHub. Fetch latest release.\n159\t3. If release has an asset matching `entire-<name>_<os>_<arch>(.exe)?` →\n160\t   binary install.\n161\t4. Else → git-clone install (script plugin). Verify executable of same name\n162\t   as the directory exists and is `+x`.\n163\t5. Conflict check: `rootCmd.Find([]string{name})` must return root or the\n164\t   extension group; otherwise refuse with an error pointing at\n165\t   `entire plugin exec`.\n166\t6. Atomic placement: download/clone to `entire-<name>.tmp`, rename to final.\n167\t\n168\t## Upgrade\n169\t\n170\t- **Binary** — refetch latest release, replace binary atomically, rewrite\n171\t  manifest.\n172\t- **Script** — `git -C <dir> pull --ff-only` (or\n173\t  `git reset --hard origin/HEAD` with `--force`).\n174\t- **Local** — no-op (warn).\n175\t- **Pinned** — skip unless `--force`.\n176\t\n177\t## Milestones (independently mergeable)\n178\t\n179\t1. **Skeleton.** Storage, manager, classification, `list`, `remove`. Tests\n180\t   with hand-placed fake plugins of all three kinds.\n181\t2. **Dispatch.** All three kinds, Unix + Windows. Argv passthrough, exit-code\n182\t   propagation, stdio inheritance, `ENTIRE_*` env injection. Tests via\n183\t   `execx.NonInteractive` against fake plugins.\n184\t3. **Install — binary path.** GitHub release fetch with a mocked `httptest`\n185\t   server. Conflict check against `rootCmd.Find()`. Atomic swap.\n186\t4. **Install — git path + local.** Shell out to the `git` CLI (consistent\n187\t   with Entire's existing carve-out for go-git v5 quirks). `.` → symlink.\n188\t5. **Upgrade.** Both kinds, `--force` flag, pin handling.\n189\t6. **`entire plugin exec`.** Tiny; routes through dispatcher with built-in\n190\t   precedence bypassed.\n191\t7. **`entire plugin create`.** `bash` (default) and `go` (with GitHub Actions\n192\t   release workflow) templates under `create/templates/`. Embedded via\n193\t   `embed.FS`. `--precompiled=other` writes a minimal language-agnostic\n194\t   scaffold.\n195\t8. **Search + browse + pin.** Topic-based dis